        "statement": "Assume $\\mathrm{AC}_\\omega$. For a nonempty oriented link $L$, the diagram quandle presentations from any two regular oriented diagrams of $L$ are isomorphic by the local quandle Tietze transformations for R1, R2 and R3. If $L=K$ has one component and $D$ is its diagram, let\n$$W(D)=\\langle g_a\\ (a\\in A(D))\\mid g_v=g_o^{-1}g_ug_o\\text{ at every crossing with source }u,\\text{ target }v,\\text{ and overarc }o\\rangle.$$\nThen the positive-meridian Wirtinger constructor uses these same under-arcs and crossing relations, and\n$$\\operatorname{Adj}(Q(D))\\cong W(D)\\cong\\pi_1(S^3\\setminus K).$$\nNo completeness or knot-classification assertion is made."
      },
      {
        "id": "thm-rack-colorings-are-framed-invariants",
        "kind": "theorem",
        "title": "Rack colorings are framed Reidemeister invariants",
        "deps": [
