            },
            {
              "title": "J. Scott Carter, A Survey of Quandle Ideas, §2, arXiv:1002.4429v2, pp. 3–8",
              "url": "https://arxiv.org/pdf/1002.4429"
            }
          ]
        },
        "statement": "Assume $\\mathrm{AC}_\\omega$ for the smooth framing statements. Let $R$ be a rack and let $\\pi(x)=x*x$ be its kink map. Rack-coloring sets\nare in bijection across every oriented R2 or R3 move and planar isotopy.\nAcross a single oriented R1 curl, the label transported along the affected\nstrand changes by $\\pi$ or $\\pi^{-1}$ according to the curl orientation.\nConsequently, an opposite-kink pair on the same component whose two signed framing changes cancel\ninduces a bijection on colorings. A single unframed R1 move has a unique\nextension for every boundary color exactly when $\\pi$ is the identity, which\nis the quandle idempotency axiom. Thus finite rack coloring counts are\ninvariant under R2, R3, planar isotopy, and framing-preserving opposite-kink\ncompensation; the unframed R1 move is covered when the rack is a quandle."
      }
